{"name":"Bittersweet","hex":"#fea051","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bittersweet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Both bitter and sweet.","Expressing contrasting emotions of pain and pleasure."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Bittersweet nightshade (Solanum dulcamara).","Bittersweetness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bittersweet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Solanum dulcamara","blocks":[{"text":"Solanum dulcamara is a species of vine in the genus Solanum of the family Solanaceae. Common names include bittersweet, bittersweet nightshade, bitter nightshade, blue bindweed, Amara Dulcis, climbing nightshade, felonwort, fellenwort, felonwood, poisonberry, poisonflower, scarlet berry, snakeberry, trailing bittersweet, trailing nightshade, violet bloom, and woody nightshade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Solanum_dulcamara_%285386574212%29.jpg/330px-Solanum_dulcamara_%285386574212%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solanum_dulcamara","wikidata":"Q147707"},{"title":"Celastrus scandens","blocks":[{"text":"Celastrus scandens, commonly called American bittersweet, is a species of bittersweet that blooms mostly in June and is commonly found on rich, well-drained soils of woodlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Celastrus_scandens_fruit.jpg/330px-Celastrus_scandens_fruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Celastrus_scandens","wikidata":"Q469628"},{"title":"Bittersweet (Madison Beer song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Bittersweet\" is a song recorded by American singer Madison Beer for her third studio album, Locket (2026). It was released by Sing It Loud and Epic Records on October 10, 2025, as the third single from the album. It was written and produced by Beer and One Love, with additional writing from Madi Yanofsky and Jon Robert Hall. A synth-pop track, \"Bittersweet\" is about moving on from a failed relationship."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Madison_Beer_-_Bittersweet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bittersweet_(Madison_Beer_song)","wikidata":"Q136805109"},{"title":"List of Crayola crayon colors","blocks":[{"text":"Since the introduction of Crayola drawing crayons by Binney & Smith in 1903, more than 200 colors have been produced in a wide variety of assortments. The table below represents all of the colors found in regular Crayola assortments from 1903 to the present. Since the introduction of fluorescent crayons in the 1970s, the standard colors have been complemented by a number of specialty crayon assortments, represented in subsequent tables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Crayola1.jpg/330px-Crayola1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Crayola_crayon_colors","wikidata":"Q6568034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Solanum_dulcamara%2C_Fogner%2C_Oslo..JPG/250px-Solanum_dulcamara%2C_Fogner%2C_Oslo..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Solanum_dulcamara%2C_Fogner%2C_Oslo..JPG/500px-Solanum_dulcamara%2C_Fogner%2C_Oslo..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Solanum_dulcamara%2C_Fogner%2C_Oslo..JPG/250px-Solanum_dulcamara%2C_Fogner%2C_Oslo..JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolanum_dulcamara%2C_Fogner%2C_Oslo..JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Bitters